WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.888
- My name's Robbie,

00:00:00.888 --> 00:00:03.526
and I'm gonna meet my
birth mother this weekend.

00:00:03.526 --> 00:00:08.485
(acoustic guitar music)

00:00:08.485 --> 00:00:10.907
My parents were open about
the adoption my whole life.

00:00:10.907 --> 00:00:11.659
I didn't really care,

00:00:11.659 --> 00:00:13.711
'cause the adoptive
parents were my parents,

00:00:13.711 --> 00:00:14.767
and I didn't think any other way.

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:15.946
I have never met my birth mother.

00:00:15.946 --> 00:00:17.348
My brother hadn't either,

00:00:17.348 --> 00:00:19.298
but we're blood related,
so it's the same mother.

00:00:19.298 --> 00:00:21.088
I got the three little facts.

00:00:21.088 --> 00:00:23.648
Her name, where she used to
live, and her maiden name.

00:00:23.648 --> 00:00:25.170
It blew my mind that, honestly,

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.000
with little tid-bits of information,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.518
you could find someone on the internet.

00:00:28.518 --> 00:00:33.210
(acoustic guitar music)

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.853
I'm excited to go out with my brother,

00:00:34.853 --> 00:00:36.892
and take a journey and meet her.

00:00:36.892 --> 00:00:38.432
It's too early!

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.035
Just landed!

00:00:42.035 --> 00:00:42.787
This is Doug.

00:00:42.787 --> 00:00:43.842
- I'm Doug.

00:00:43.842 --> 00:00:45.374
- My brother.

00:00:45.374 --> 00:00:46.613
Same birth mother.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.096
Same adoptive family.

00:00:48.096 --> 00:00:49.193
- I am a little nervous.

00:00:49.193 --> 00:00:52.505
Basically, get to kinda, you know,

00:00:52.505 --> 00:00:55.167
see a different lens of
what my life could've been.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:58.824
- [Robbie] What do you
think of this whole journey?

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:02.260
- I think it's probably
gonna be a shit show,

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:04.208
but I really hope it's not,

00:01:04.208 --> 00:01:07.442
'cause like, you guys don't deserve that.

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:10.766
And listening to the conversations
that you've had with her,

00:01:10.766 --> 00:01:14.309
like, I don't know,

00:01:14.309 --> 00:01:15.987
'cause she doesn't sound that interested

00:01:15.987 --> 00:01:19.516
in meeting you guys.

00:01:19.516 --> 00:01:20.559
- [Robbie] Yeah.

00:01:20.559 --> 00:01:21.717
- Yeah.

00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:25.395
- It's the night before we go

00:01:25.395 --> 00:01:27.630
and meet Suzanne, my birth mother.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.535
And feeling-wise,

00:01:30.535 --> 00:01:33.217
I think I'm more nervous
than I've ever been

00:01:33.217 --> 00:01:36.976
about meeting someone or
doing something before.

00:01:36.976 --> 00:01:38.764
We're gonna understand where we came from,

00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:40.491
and why we were given up,

00:01:40.491 --> 00:01:44.250
and why we were lucky enough to

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.668
be adopted by such a great family.

00:01:46.668 --> 00:01:48.923
But it was kinda hard
to get a read on her,

00:01:48.923 --> 00:01:51.361
the last couple of times I
talked to her on the phone,

00:01:51.361 --> 00:01:54.043
because she, she just, I don't know,

00:01:54.043 --> 00:01:56.298
she didn't seem as excited
as Doug and I were.

00:01:56.298 --> 00:01:57.253
We'd be like, "Can't wait to see you!"

00:01:57.253 --> 00:01:58.716
And she'd be like, "Oh, okay."

00:01:58.716 --> 00:02:03.510
So, I guess, going into
this, I'm not really sure

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.927
where her mind is at.

00:02:05.927 --> 00:02:08.099
So, we just got off the highway,

00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:12.305
and we're kinda in, I
guess southwest Pueblo.

00:02:12.305 --> 00:02:15.952
I guess we'll park here and walk in.

00:02:15.952 --> 00:02:17.537
(acoustic guitar music)

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:18.451
Suzanne?

00:02:18.451 --> 00:02:22.511
(acoustic guitar music)

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:29.341
It's nice to meet you!

00:02:29.341 --> 00:02:30.337
- Which one are you?

00:02:30.337 --> 00:02:31.515
- I'm Robbie.

00:02:31.515 --> 00:02:32.430
- Doug.

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.502
- Oh, alright!

00:02:34.502 --> 00:02:35.315
- How are you?

00:02:35.315 --> 00:02:37.422
- Alright.

00:02:37.422 --> 00:02:38.525
- How are you?

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.500
- Alright.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.170
- Yeah?

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.775
Wow.

00:02:41.775 --> 00:02:43.015
I actually got to meet you.

00:02:43.015 --> 00:02:44.505
- Yeah!

00:02:44.505 --> 00:02:49.472
(acoustic guitar music)

00:02:49.472 --> 00:02:51.422
- This was me in my younger days.

00:02:51.422 --> 00:02:54.306
That's when Chrissy was
about seven or eight.

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:57.210
And this is Charlie when he was--

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.715
- Wow, that is,

00:02:58.715 --> 00:03:01.229
that is uncanny!

00:03:01.229 --> 00:03:03.022
- Here's Pat.

00:03:03.022 --> 00:03:05.415
I don't have too many
pictures of him left.

00:03:05.415 --> 00:03:07.935
- Yeah, see you're gonna
have no hair in a few years.

00:03:07.935 --> 00:03:08.829
(laughter)

00:03:08.829 --> 00:03:10.251
You're gonna do what I do!

00:03:10.251 --> 00:03:11.165
(laughter)

00:03:11.165 --> 00:03:12.405
So, this is the first time I've ever seen

00:03:12.405 --> 00:03:16.446
a picture of our birth father.

00:03:16.446 --> 00:03:20.470
- This is Chrissy when she was 17.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:22.847
My mother was very poor,

00:03:22.847 --> 00:03:25.448
and she had eight kids.

00:03:25.448 --> 00:03:27.459
We ended up in a children's home,

00:03:27.459 --> 00:03:29.755
and my mother died at 16.

00:03:29.755 --> 00:03:31.245
- Wow.

00:03:31.245 --> 00:03:33.134
- Then I got involved with pot,

00:03:33.134 --> 00:03:36.376
which was a train ride through hell,

00:03:36.376 --> 00:03:38.660
is the only answer.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:40.480
When you guys came along,

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:44.808
you were supposed to stay
with me in this family,

00:03:44.808 --> 00:03:49.541
and I had Robbie to give you a companion.

00:03:49.541 --> 00:03:51.838
It wasn't an accident.

00:03:51.838 --> 00:03:53.687
Robbie wasn't an accident.

00:03:53.687 --> 00:03:55.948
For me, you know,

00:03:55.948 --> 00:03:59.098
I don't look at them as they're my kids,

00:03:59.098 --> 00:04:00.256
'cause they're not.

00:04:00.256 --> 00:04:03.263
I look at myself as a surrogate mother.

00:04:03.263 --> 00:04:07.448
I was an instrument to get them in here,

00:04:07.448 --> 00:04:10.374
so they could get their lessons done.

00:04:10.374 --> 00:04:14.214
And so, we're strangers,

00:04:14.214 --> 00:04:15.636
is what we are.

00:04:15.636 --> 00:04:17.017
- I mean, everything we know about you,

00:04:17.017 --> 00:04:20.086
I think we've learned in the past month.

00:04:20.086 --> 00:04:20.593
- Yeah!

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.346
- Yeah.

00:04:21.346 --> 00:04:24.501
- When I went to court for,

00:04:24.501 --> 00:04:29.147
not court, but the judge's
chamber for Robbie,

00:04:29.147 --> 00:04:32.322
the judge says,

00:04:32.322 --> 00:04:36.914
"You release all claims to these kids."

00:04:36.914 --> 00:04:39.120
And I thought, "That was rotten!"

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.090
'Cause when we first made the deal,

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:44.118
it was supposed to be an open adoption,

00:04:44.118 --> 00:04:47.408
and Bruce and Anne closed it.

00:04:47.408 --> 00:04:48.832
- Do you know why they did that?

00:04:48.832 --> 00:04:52.691
- Yeah, 'cause I was very
unstable back in those times.

00:04:52.691 --> 00:04:53.281
- Mm-hmm.

00:04:53.281 --> 00:04:54.643
- And I know I was.

00:04:54.643 --> 00:04:57.596
- Do you think it was for
the best that that happened?

00:04:57.596 --> 00:04:58.929
- Probably so!

00:04:58.929 --> 00:05:00.148
Probably so.

00:05:00.148 --> 00:05:01.835
- We're extremely thankful for--

00:05:01.835 --> 00:05:04.189
- Grateful for the
chance that you gave us.

00:05:04.189 --> 00:05:06.912
The opportunity to do
something with our lives.

00:05:06.912 --> 00:05:08.639
- I'm happy to see where you're at,

00:05:08.639 --> 00:05:12.519
because you fulfilled my deal with God.

00:05:12.519 --> 00:05:15.282
'Cause I wanted a better education,

00:05:15.282 --> 00:05:18.323
a better life, which
Anne and Bruce gave you,

00:05:18.323 --> 00:05:19.725
and nice jobs.

00:05:19.725 --> 00:05:20.781
And you did.

00:05:20.781 --> 00:05:25.519
(acoustic guitar music)

00:05:29.193 --> 00:05:30.595
Well--

00:05:30.595 --> 00:05:31.590
- It's great seeing you.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:33.196
- Yeah, good seeing you guys.

00:05:33.196 --> 00:05:34.332
You take care.

00:05:34.332 --> 00:05:35.654
- Yeah, we'll definitely keep in touch.

00:05:35.654 --> 00:05:36.445
- It was great to meet you.

00:05:36.445 --> 00:05:38.600
- Uh-huh, great meeting you!

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.104
- I feel good about the experience.

00:05:40.104 --> 00:05:41.526
- Good, it was a great experience.

00:05:41.526 --> 00:05:43.009
I think the thing that
sticks out the most,

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:46.443
was just her, her strength
to be able to do this,

00:05:46.443 --> 00:05:48.596
and to be able recognize that, you know,

00:05:48.596 --> 00:05:51.075
she's in a very difficult situation,

00:05:51.075 --> 00:05:53.635
and to be able to look beyond that,

00:05:53.635 --> 00:05:56.563
and see what, you know,
she thought was a way out,

00:05:56.563 --> 00:05:59.225
that would give us a chance.

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:00.932
Just the strength to be able to do that

00:06:00.932 --> 00:06:02.454
is very impressive to me.

00:06:02.454 --> 00:06:04.176
- I wouldn't mind having her in my life.

00:06:04.176 --> 00:06:05.801
- Yeah!

00:06:05.801 --> 00:06:06.946
- Yeah.

00:06:06.946 --> 00:06:08.307
- It's good to keep in touch with her,

00:06:08.307 --> 00:06:10.542
let her know how we're doing.

00:06:10.542 --> 00:06:12.594
- She did an amazing thing for us,

00:06:12.594 --> 00:06:16.921
so if we can give back a little anything,

00:06:16.921 --> 00:06:18.734
I mean, I think she more than warrants it.

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:20.685
- I think that we're
smiling after we do this

00:06:20.685 --> 00:06:23.883
says a lot about, you know,
how this weekend went.

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:28.746
(smooth music)

00:06:28.746 --> 00:06:29.933
(swoosh)

00:06:29.933 --> 00:06:31.605
(squeaking)

